---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="AI-first CAD for engineers"
  description="AI-first CAD for engineers. Describe an intended change, let an agent work in the open model, then review editable features and measurements alongside the rest of your engineering work."
>
  <header class="home-hero">
    <div class="wrap home-hero-grid">
      <div class="home-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Engineering workspace · Browser and desktop</p>
        <h1>AI-first CAD for engineers.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Describe the change you intend. An agent works in the open model, then you review editable features and measurements before saving a revision.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/gallery/">See product work</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/product/">Explore the product</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="home-hero-facts" aria-label="Product fundamentals">
          <li>Exact B-rep solids</li>
          <li>Editable feature history</li>
          <li>Measurements for engineering review</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="home-hero-media">
        <a href="/gallery/#modeling" aria-label="View the modeling workspace in the gallery">
          <img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1600" height="900" alt="Chudware modeling workspace showing a parametric enclosure and its editable feature tree" fetchpriority="high" />
        </a>
        <figcaption><span>Modeling example</span><a href="/gallery/#modeling">Request and result</a></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section home-ai" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI in the engineering loop</p>
        <h2 id="ai-title">Describe the intent. Review the result.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Brief the intended change and constraints. The copilot uses normal modeling tools in the open document, and its sketches and features stay editable in the same feature tree.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/ai-copilot/">Read the AI copilot guide</a></div>
      </header>
      <ol class="home-ai-steps" aria-label="AI copilot workflow">
        <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Connect</strong><p>Connect a supported provider account or add an API key issued by the provider.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Describe</strong><p>Name the intended change, critical dimensions, and what must not change.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Review</strong><p>Inspect editable features and check critical measurements before saving a revision.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section home-capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">One engineering environment</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-title">Move from geometry to a documented result.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each workspace stays connected to the same project, model, and revision history.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article><p class="capability-index">01</p><h3><a href="/product/modeling/">Modeling</a></h3><p>Constrained sketches and ordered features produce editable exact solids.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">02</p><h3><a href="/product/assemblies/">Assemblies</a></h3><p>Locate components with mates, then inspect motion, clearance, and interference.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">03</p><h3><a href="/product/simulation/">Simulation</a></h3><p>Set up structural, modal, and thermal studies against the active design.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">04</p><h3><a href="/product/cam/">CAM</a></h3><p>Define stock, tools, and operations, simulate removal, and post G-code.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">05</p><h3>Electronics</h3><p>Keep electronics and firmware workspaces alongside the mechanical project.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">06</p><h3><a href="/product/plm/">PLM</a></h3><p>Keep revisions, project files, manufacturing artifacts, and decisions together.</p></article>
        <article><p class="capability-index">07</p><h3><a href="/docs/ai-copilot/">AI</a></h3><p>Give an agent the open model as context and inspect the features it creates.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section home-work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading home-work-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Product gallery</p>
          <h2 id="work-title">Modeling, CAM, and simulation in view.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/gallery/">Open the gallery</a>
      </header>
      <div class="home-work-grid">
        <figure>
          <a href="/gallery/#cam"><img src="/images/cam.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace with a CAM job, operations, and toolpath simulation" /></a>
          <figcaption><span><strong>CAM</strong> · Operations and toolpath simulation</span><a href="/gallery/#cam">View full image</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a href="/gallery/#simulation"><img src="/images/fea.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="Chudware simulation workspace with a static stress result, legend, and result summary" /></a>
          <figcaption><span><strong>Simulation</strong> · Static stress result</span><a href="/gallery/#simulation">View full image</a></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start with the product</p>
      <h2>Open Chudware in your browser.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Create an account for the browser workspace, or review the documentation first.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
